{"title":"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A coin that comes up heads with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/b/19bf07ceb43df8c7388742c5c1a3667791306791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> and tails with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/81215317764c911fc434035b2a17ebe7b6a9944c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 - p &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" /> independently on each flip is flipped <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times. Suppose that the probability of three heads and five tails is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/5/1b554d974c0d5d304c2f7d384d6d709b2e4dab2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {1}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> of the probability of five heads and three tails. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebfcc7b528b634fdeabcbd3f8c609dc4283fe484.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = \\frac {m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"52\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The probability of three heads and five tails is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f6bd0f212777fc92993606f224a5a0a2fae25b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom {8}{3}p^3(1-p)^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"114\" height=\"53\" /> and the probability of five heads and three tails is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/639818c66880d463e0ef6cefcc52ea96257d0fdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom {8}{3}p^5(1-p)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"114\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/0/30069ba36d4c486c86a61a1a7d9595a0aead324f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 25\\binom {8}{3}p^3(1-p)^5&amp;=\\binom {8}{3}p^5(1-p)^3 \\\\ 25(1-p)^2&amp;=p^2 \\\\ 25p^2-50p+25&amp;=p^2 \\\\ 24p^2-50p+25&amp;=0 \\\\ p&amp;=\\frac {5}{6}\\end{align*}\" width=\"272\" height=\"180\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/f/4ef035d855566cebeb1d2df40b0e9df191976438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+6=\\boxed{011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We start as shown above. However, when we get to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/3/d13a815d2dfb759301f3f4f169789822d1828cfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25(1-p)^2=p^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"19\" />, we square root both sides to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09d79c189d5268196bc4bffcd039f56d9de09e9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5(1-p)=p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />. We can do this because we know that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/d/5fdd66831cbbb8238ab62234975610d1682bbb03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" /> are between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so they are both positive. Now, we have: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/c/05c528279191df36d09477fb604ea5f02596322c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 5(1-p)&amp;=p \\\\ 5-5p&amp;=p \\\\ 5&amp;=6p \\\\ p&amp;=\\frac {5}{6}\\end{align*}\" width=\"105\" height=\"112\" />\n</p><p>Now, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/f/4ef035d855566cebeb1d2df40b0e9df191976438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+6=\\boxed{011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Jerry_Guo\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rewrite it as&#160;: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/0/5e02ec3a09c570d321bfa4e3b6baf2e6d39b8714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(P)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"19\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/f/cefd27b1692f83d7c46a26cfef13e16681fe0788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-P)^5=\\frac {1}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"112\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/574ce04e987704e38dbd6f1bf7476f0281f6f0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(P)^5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"19\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e564490dd6b75e91676c5560609b62a2c0c8ad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-P)^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>This can be simplified as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/c/2fcdaea8b7e02b24f34bf0b3433b7724e6caed79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24P^2 -50P + 25 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"167\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>This can be factored into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffa691aef9e9b9292dcff497bf8300a1b3b25d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4P-5)(6P-5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This yields two solutions: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0af5e1b6cfb1551ce48c49f840977c850c64b248.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac54$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> (ignored because it would result in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10da81d3c8f59d02c4e922364aa44d72ad763824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-p&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />  ) or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be4a2f0e5db740f16b3fefc0866ae53f3d75ea43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/4/514e465ce618e72a5c735984edf73e15d28cb57f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/616db6fac5c4e3f66e28fff9d58f1adcd6a074a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {011}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/NL79UexadzE\">https://youtu.be/NL79UexadzE</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P00iOJdQiL4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P00iOJdQiL4</a>\n</p><p>~Shreyas S\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I\" title=\"2009 AIME I\">2009 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2009\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017170947\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 240/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5772/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.627      1 -total\n 58.73%    7.416      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.49%    4.987      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7984:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017170947 and revision id 169987. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}